nodes.detail:
**Execute:** produce an SRT with local transcription (Whisper via whisper.cpp, NVIDIA Parakeet) or a speech API;
estimate per-word timings from SRT segments; list the on-screen text of every clip in the plan before building;
style captions with the design system's typeface and keep them clear of panels. clawd-video defaults to no captions
unless asked, which suits wordless shorts.

**Why it raises quality:** the transcript is the sync backbone for anything keyed to speech, and readable captions
widen reach on social platforms.

**Failure modes:** first drafts forgot subtitles entirely; the b-roll skill cannot transcribe on its own;
transcription models need network access to download weights; captions colliding with graphics.

**Pattern (clawd-video):** 1920x1080, 24 fps, 8 to 20 s, sound on, no captions, one set; five beats for 15 s; merge
beats rather than rush; for existing characters, find an accurate reference first and write proportions as numbers;
deliver with an honest verification summary.

**Why it works:** removes interrogation friction while keeping the user in control of anything they specify;
complements the inputs block, which asks only when a field truly matters.

**Combine with the inputs block:** a field the user leaves empty takes the default and is stated back in the plan, so the user can override it at the plan gate rather than being interrupted at the start.
